{"id":"ce1461d3e7bc342b","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-finite-residual-characterization.md","title":"Myhill–Nerode Theorem","display":"thm-myhill-nerode — Myhill–Nerode Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-finite-residual-characterization","aliases":["73-thm-finite-residual-characterization","73-thm-myhill-nerode"],"display":"thm-myhill-nerode — Myhill–Nerode Theorem","depends_on":["[[73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa]]","[[73-df-language-residual-equivalence]]","[[73-df-finite-automaton-language-class]]","[[73-df-language-pumping-length]]"],"source_id":"HMU2007","source_ref":"§4.4, print pp. 155–165; PDF pp. 177–187; local quotient/finite-index formulation","source_status":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate","reviewed_on":"2026-10-24","legacy_source_id":"HU1979","legacy_source_ref":"§3.4, Theorems 3.9–3.10, pp. 65–71; minimum-state count distinguished from minimum pumping length","legacy_source_status":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review","revision_round":"pdf-third-edition-20261024","edition_role":"third-edition-core","third_edition_chapter":4},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-finite-residual-characterization"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-finite-residual-characterization</span><span>73-thm-myhill-nerode</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-myhill-nerode — Myhill–Nerode Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e6c2dfbed164fa58\" href=\"?note=e6c2dfbed164fa58\" title=\"73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa\">73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f41b3be50448ef3b\" href=\"?note=f41b3be50448ef3b\" title=\"73-df-language-residual-equivalence\">73-df-language-residual-equivalence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c284ffb568a496fd\" href=\"?note=c284ffb568a496fd\" title=\"73-df-finite-automaton-language-class\">73-df-finite-automaton-language-class</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" href=\"?note=01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" title=\"73-df-language-pumping-length\">73-df-language-pumping-length</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_id","html":"HMU2007"},{"key":"source_ref","html":"§4.4, print pp. 155–165; PDF pp. 177–187; local quotient/finite-index formulation"},{"key":"source_status","html":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate"},{"key":"reviewed_on","html":"2026-10-24"},{"key":"legacy_source_id","html":"HU1979"},{"key":"legacy_source_ref","html":"§3.4, Theorems 3.9–3.10, pp. 65–71; minimum-state count distinguished from minimum pumping length"},{"key":"legacy_source_status","html":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review"},{"key":"revision_round","html":"pdf-third-edition-20261024"},{"key":"edition_role","html":"third-edition-core"},{"key":"third_edition_chapter","html":"4"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (alphabet)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\">\\(L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\)</span> (language)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ind}(L)\">\\(\\operatorname{ind}(L)\\)</span> (Myhill–Nerode index, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"f41b3be50448ef3b\" href=\"?note=f41b3be50448ef3b\" title=\"73-df-language-residual-equivalence\">73-df-language-residual-equivalence</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_{\\mathsf{reg}}:\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\to\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\">\\(p_{\\mathsf{reg}}:\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\to\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" href=\"?note=01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" title=\"73-df-language-pumping-length\">73-df-language-pumping-length</a>；仅在第二个断言量化的正则语言上取值，不对任意 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\">\\(L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\)</span> 预设该值存在。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L)\">\\(\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L)\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"e6c2dfbed164fa58\" href=\"?note=e6c2dfbed164fa58\" title=\"73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa\">73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa</a>，仅在有限指数的语言上调用。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ind}(L)&lt;\\aleph_0\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ind}(L)&lt;\\aleph_0\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\;\np_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)=\\operatorname{ind}(L)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\;\np_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)=\\operatorname{ind}(L)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall L\\in\\{A\\subseteq\\Sigma^*:\\operatorname{ind}(A)&lt;\\aleph_0\\}\\;[L(\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L))=L\\land|\\pi_1(\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L))|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall L\\in\\{A\\subseteq\\Sigma^*:\\operatorname{ind}(A)&lt;\\aleph_0\\}\\;[L(\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L))=L\\land|\\pi_1(\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L))|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every DFA state reached by a prefix determines one right quotient, so any recognizing DFA has at least <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ind}(L)\">\\(\\operatorname{ind}(L)\\)</span> reachable states.</li>\n<li>When the index is finite, the equivalence classes themselves form a DFA with transition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[x]_L\\xrightarrow{a}[xa]_L\">\\([x]_L\\xrightarrow{a}[xa]_L\\)</span>. This DFA is minimal.</li>\n<li>The former unconditional equation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|Q_M|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)\">\\(|Q_M|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)\\)</span> was false for nonminimal DFAs and has been replaced by the minimum-state statement.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa","status":"resolved","id":"e6c2dfbed164fa58","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-residual-equivalence","status":"resolved","id":"f41b3be50448ef3b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-language-residual-equivalence]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-finite-automaton-language-class","status":"resolved","id":"c284ffb568a496fd","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-finite-automaton-language-class]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-pumping-length","status":"resolved","id":"01b7b9d9615ddaa5","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-language-pumping-length]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-residual-equivalence","status":"resolved","id":"f41b3be50448ef3b","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ind}(L)$ (Myhill–Nerode index, see [[73-df-language-residual-equivalence]])","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-pumping-length","status":"resolved","id":"01b7b9d9615ddaa5","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$p_{\\mathsf{reg}}:\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\to\\mathbb N_{>0}$ 见 [[73-df-language-pumping-length]]；仅在第二个断言量化的正则语言上取值，不对任意 $L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*$ 预设该值存在。","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa","status":"resolved","id":"e6c2dfbed164fa58","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L)$ 见 [[73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa]]，仅在有限指数的语言上调用。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ind}(L)","display":false},{"tex":"p_{\\mathsf{reg}}:\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\to\\mathbb N_{>0}","display":false},{"tex":"L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ind}(L)<\\aleph_0\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\;\np_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)=\\operatorname{ind}(L)","display":true},{"tex":"\\forall L\\in\\{A\\subseteq\\Sigma^*:\\operatorname{ind}(A)<\\aleph_0\\}\\;[L(\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L))=L\\land|\\pi_1(\\operatorname{NerodeDFA}(L))|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)]","display":true},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ind}(L)","display":false},{"tex":"[x]_L\\xrightarrow{a}[xa]_L","display":false},{"tex":"|Q_M|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)","display":false}],"bytes":2573,"backlinks":[{"id":"6af52783a9bce985","anchor":"ref-66","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[73-thm-finite-residual-characterization|Myhill–Nerode Theorem]]"},{"id":"9b1dba6be30381aa","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"固定字母表 $\\Sigma$。$M=(Q,\\Sigma,\\delta,q_0,F)$、$N=(P,\\Sigma,\\eta,p_0,H)$ 是 DFA。$h:Q\\to P$；$\\operatorname{MinimalDFA}_{\\Sigma}$ 与 $\\operatorname{DFAIso}$ 在下式定义。语言、最小化及指数见 [[73-df-dfa-minimization-construction]]、[[73-df-nerode-canonical-dfa]]、[[73-thm-finite-residual-characterization]]。"},{"id":"69901fc0f2bc2a70","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["e6c2dfbed164fa58","f41b3be50448ef3b","c284ffb568a496fd","01b7b9d9615ddaa5"]}